/-!
# Four-category block grammar: capture, ranks, profiles and the exception

Data for `Rule30GrammarRuns`. A block `1^r 0^q` is admissible when `r = 1, q ≥ 10`, `r = 2, q ≥ 8`,
`r = 4, q ≥ 7`, or `r ≥ 9, q ≥ 9`. Strips are the fourteen cells right of the center, with an arbitrary
cell beyond them at every step (`Rule30StripCertificates`). `capture0` … `capture3` move every strip
through `A1`, `A2`, `A3` into the envelope `E` (`16384 → 2288 → 1915 → 1797 → 1791` strips) under any
admissible block, and `nested1` … `nested4` show the stages are nested. `partition` splits `E` into
the rank regions `R0` … `R6` (sizes `1386, 339, 44, 13, 2, 5, 2`); `advance…` and `target…` show that
no admissible block raises the rank and that from ranks `1` … `5` every block lowers it; `exit6`
shows that from `R6` every block with `r ≠ 4` lowers it. `profile` gives column `1` along the white
run after `r` black steps from `R0`: white for `delay r` steps, then black (`delay = 2, 0, 0` for
`r = 1, 2, 4`, and `1` for `r ≥ 9`, through the black-closed set `L`). `exception6` gives the same
for `1^4` from `R6`, with delay `1`.
-/

set_option Elab.async false

set_option maxRecDepth 100000

set_option maxHeartbeats 0

namespace Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30GrammarData

open Rule30StripCertificates Rule30RunEnvelopes Rule30LongWhiteSupport Rule30FastImage

theorem partition (s : Nat) (hs : s<2^14) (hm : E.testBit s=true) : rank s<7 ∧ (region (rank s)).testBit s=true := by
  simpa only [Nat.zero_add,Bool.and_eq_true,decide_eq_true_eq] using checkMask_spec _ 14 0 E partitionCheck s hs hm

